Support multiple shipments per order, move Purchase Orders into Sales,
add date-range/search everywhere, cross-link order to its history, add
Carton Summary and clipboard copy to Delivery History (v0.105)

Multiple shipments per order:
- New Shipment entity/table (V50 migration) - a snapshot of one
  completed shipment (shippingCost, courierMethod, dpdNetworkKey, and if
  DPD-booked its dpdShipmentId/dpdConsignmentNumber/dpdParcelNumbers/
  dpdShippedAt), written the moment that shipment is about to be
  superseded by another.
- OrderService.update(): archives the order's current shipment fields
  into a Shipment row and clears the order's own dpd* booking fields
  whenever reopening for an extra shipment - covers both reopening from
  a fully locked order (Invoice Pending/Completed) and reopening an
  already-Partially-Despatched order that already has its own shipment
  booked (a third-or-later shipment), via a new reopeningForExtraShipment
  condition (broader than the wasLocked check the status-lock rejection
  logic still uses). Clearing the dpd fields means DespatchService's
  existing "already booked, skip" check naturally books a genuinely new
  DPD shipment on the next despatch confirmation, with no changes needed
  in DespatchService itself.
- Delivery History detail: new "Previous Shipments" section (backend:
  ShipmentRepository, ShipmentView DTO, DeliveryHistoryDetailView gains
  previousShipments) listing every earlier shipment with its own Track
  link.

Purchase Orders moved into the Sales nav group (Layout.tsx) - no route
or functional change, just where it's found.

Date range + search added to Sales Activity (order date), Invoice
History (invoice date), Payment Tracking (invoice date), RMAs (submitted
date, and RMAs didn't have a search box before either), and Purchase
Orders (created date, ditto no search box before). New shared
DateRangePicker component and utils/format.ts:inDateRange() - all of
these already pull their full dataset into the browser, same as
Delivery History's own search, so this filters client-side rather than
adding new backend query params.

OrderEdit: "Delivery History →" and "Invoice History →" pills next to
the existing support-ticket pill, shown once the order has actually
reached those stages, linking through pre-filtered to that order number
(hasInvoices checked against the real invoice list, not guessed from
order status).

Delivery History detail page:
- Carton Summary dropdown above the item table - per-carton SKU
  quantities, always exact regardless of packing mode (new
  DeliveryHistoryCartonSummaryRow DTO/query, built from the same two
  data sources as the per-unit view but summed rather than attributed).
- A search box for the item table (SKU, product, MAC, serial, batch).
- Clipboard-copy icons on the MAC Address/Serial Number column headers -
  copies every value currently shown in that column (respects the
  search box), one per line.

CHANGELOG.md, README.md and the User Guide PDF updated to match; the
"can't have a second DPD shipment" known limitation noted in v0.104's
changelog is resolved by this release.

